{"id":"0edd48cf9a6e56110497d2444a9b5bf36d8c914d","axis":"silent","repo":"elastic/elasticsearch","sha":"0edd48cf9a6e56110497d2444a9b5bf36d8c914d","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/changelog/162687.yaml","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@","+area: ES|QL","+issues: []","+pr: 162687","+summary: \"ESQL:DS: Authorize datasets named by received compute plans\"","+type: enhancement"],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"x-pack/plugin/esql/build.gradle","lines":["@@ -37,6 +37,34 @@ base {","   archivesName = 'x-pack-esql'"," }"," ","+configurations {","+  /*","+   * Security and its test artifacts for DataNodeRequestDatasetAuthorizationIT. Kept out of internalClusterTestImplementation","+   * because that one is exposed to every module consuming this project's internalClusterTest artifact, and security's","+   * net.jcip:jcip-annotations defines the same classes as the com.github.stephenc.jcip:jcip-annotations that","+   * repository-azure brings: jar hell there. It extends the regular internalClusterTest dependencies, so that both","+   * resolve to one version of every library, and it replaces the regular runtime classpath of the internalClusterTest task.","+   */","+  securityIntegTest {","+    canBeConsumed = false","+    canBeResolved = true","+    extendsFrom internalClusterTestImplementation, internalClusterTestRuntimeOnly","+    def runtimeAttributes = internalClusterTestRuntimeClasspath.attributes","+    runtimeAttributes.keySet().each { attribute -> attributes.attribute(attribute, runtimeAttributes.getAttribute(attribute)) }","+  }","+}","+","+sourceSets {","+  internalClusterTest {","+    compileClasspath += configurations.securityIntegTest","+    runtimeClasspath = runtimeClasspath - configurations.internalClusterTestRuntimeClasspath + configurations.securityIntegTest","+  }","+}","+","+tasks.named('internalClusterTest').configure {","+  classpath = classpath - configurations.internalClusterTestRuntimeClasspath + configurations.securityIntegTest","+}","+"," dependencies {","   compileOnly project(':modules:lang-painless:spi')","   compileOnly project(xpackModule('ml'))","@@ -106,6 +134,9 @@ dependencies {","   internalClusterTestImplementation project(\":plugins:mapper-size\")","   internalClusterTestImplementation project(xpackModule('inference:qa:test-service-plugin'))","   internalClusterTestImplementation(testArtifact(project(xpackModule('inference'))))","+  // DataNodeRequestDatasetAuthorizationIT runs a security-enabled internal cluster against crafted compute requests.","+  securityIntegTest(testArtifact(project(xpackModule('core'))))","+  securityIntegTest(testArtifact(project(xpackModule('security'))))","   internalClusterTestImplementation project(path: xpackModule('mapper-constant-keyword'))","   internalClusterTestImplementation project(xpackModule('analytics'))","   internalClusterTestImplementation project(xpackModule('spatial'))"],"additions":31,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/internalClusterTest/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/enrich/LookupFromIndexExternalSourceIT.java","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,100 @@","+/*","+ * Copyright Elasticsearch B.V. and/or licensed to Elasticsearch B.V. under one","+ * or more contributor license agreements. Licensed under the Elastic License","+ * 2.0; you may not use this file except in compliance with the Elastic License","+ * 2.0.","+ */","+","+package org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.enrich;","+","+import org.elasticsearch.ElasticsearchStatusException;","+import org.elasticsearch.action.support.PlainActionFuture;","+import org.elasticsearch.compute.data.BlockFactory;","+import org.elasticsearch.compute.data.Page;","+import org.elasticsearch.compute.test.TestBlockFactory;","+import org.elasticsearch.index.shard.ShardId;","+import org.elasticsearch.rest.RestStatus;","+import org.elasticsearch.tasks.CancellableTask;","+import org.elasticsearch.tasks.TaskId;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.action.AbstractEsqlIntegTestCase;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.core.expression.Attribute;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.core.expression.FieldAttribute;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.core.expression.NamedExpression;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.core.tree.Source;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.core.type.DataType;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.core.type.EsField;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.datasources.spi.FileList;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.datasources.spi.SimpleSourceMetadata;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.plan.logical.ExternalRelation;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.plan.physical.FragmentExec;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.plugin.TransportEsqlQueryAction;","+","+import java.util.List;","+import java.util.Map;","+","+import static org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.EsqlTestUtils.TEST_CFG;","+import static org.hamcrest.Matchers.containsString;","+import static org.hamcrest.Matchers.is;","+","+/**","+ * The lookup service plans the pre-join plan it receives with the lookup optimizers; an external source has no place","+ * in it and nothing on that path authorizes or rebinds a dataset. A crafted lookup request carrying one must be","+ * refused before the planners see it.","+ */","+public class LookupFromIndexExternalSourceIT extends AbstractEsqlIntegTestCase {","+","+    public void testLookupPlanCarryingAnExternalSourceIsRefused() {","+        String node = randomFrom(internalCluster().getNodeNames());","+        LookupFromIndexService service = internalCluster().getInstance(TransportEsqlQueryAction.class, node).getLookupFromIndexService();","+        List<Attribute> output = List.of(","+            new FieldAttribute(Source.EMPTY, \"key\", new EsField(\"key\", DataType.INTEGER, Map.of(), true, EsField.TimeSeriesFieldType.NONE))","+        );","+        ExternalRelation relation = new ExternalRelation(","+            Source.EMPTY,","+            \"s3://attacker/whatever/*.parquet\",","+            new SimpleSourceMetadata(output, \"parquet\", \"s3://attacker/whatever/*.parquet\"),","+            output,","+            FileList.UNRESOLVED,","+            Map.of(),","+            \"secret_dataset\"","+        );","+        BlockFactory blockFactory = TestBlockFactory.getNonBreakingInstance();","+        Page inputPage = new Page(blockFactory.newConstantIntBlockWith(1, 1));","+        try {","+            LookupFromIndexService.LookupRequest request = new LookupFromIndexService.LookupRequest(","+                \"lookup-external-\" + randomAlphaOfLength(8),","+                new ShardId(\"lookup_idx\", \"uuid\", 0),","+                \"lookup_idx\",","+                inputPage,","+                null,","+                List.<NamedExpression>of(output.get(0)),","+                List.of(new MatchConfig(\"key\", 0, DataType.INTEGER)),","+                Source.EMPTY,","+                new FragmentExec(relation),","+                null,","+                randomBoolean() ? \"client-to-server\" : null,","+                null,","+                false,","+                TEST_CFG","+            );","+            CancellableTask task = new CancellableTask(","+                randomNonNegativeLong(),","+                \"transport\",","+                LookupFromIndexService.LOOKUP_ACTION_NAME,","+                \"\",","+                TaskId.EMPTY_TASK_ID,","+                Map.of()","+            );","+            PlainActionFuture<AbstractLookupService.LookupResponse> future = new PlainActionFuture<>();","+            service.doLookup(request, task, future);","+            ElasticsearchStatusException e = expectThrows(","+                ElasticsearchStatusException.class,","+                () -> future.actionGet(DEFAULT_REQUEST_TIMEOUT)","+            );","+            assertThat(e.status(), is(RestStatus.BAD_REQUEST));","+            assertThat(e.getMessage(), containsString(\"external datasets cannot be read by a lookup join\"));","+        } finally {","+            inputPage.releaseBlocks();","+        }","+    }","+}"],"additions":100,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/internalClusterTest/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plugin/DataNodeRequestDatasetAuthorizationIT.java","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,599 @@","+/*","+ * Copyright Elasticsearch B.V. and/or licensed to Elasticsearch B.V. under one","+ * or more contributor license agreements. Licensed under the Elastic License","+ * 2.0; you may not use this file except in compliance with the Elastic License","+ * 2.0.","+ */","+","+package org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.plugin;","+","+import org.apache.lucene.util.BytesRef;","+import org.elasticsearch.ElasticsearchStatusException;","+import org.elasticsearch.ExceptionsHelper;","+import org.elasticsearch.ResourceAlreadyExistsException;","+import org.elasticsearch.action.ActionListenerResponseHandler;","+import org.elasticsearch.action.support.IndicesOptions;","+import org.elasticsearch.action.support.PlainActionFuture;","+import org.elasticsearch.cluster.metadata.IndexMetadata;","+import org.elasticsearch.cluster.routing.SplitShardCountSummary;","+import org.elasticsearch.common.bytes.BytesArray;","+import org.elasticsearch.common.settings.SecureString;","+import org.elasticsearch.common.settings.Settings;","+import org.elasticsearch.common.util.concurrent.EsExecutors;","+import org.elasticsearch.common.util.concurrent.ThreadContext;","+import org.elasticsearch.compute.data.BytesRefBlock;","+import org.elasticsearch.compute.data.Page;","+import org.elasticsearch.compute.operator.exchange.ExchangeService;","+import org.elasticsearch.compute.operator.exchange.ExchangeSinkHandler;","+import org.elasticsearch.core.Nullable;","+import org.elasticsearch.core.TimeValue;","+import org.elasticsearch.index.shard.ShardId;","+import org.elasticsearch.plugins.Plugin;","+import org.elasticsearch.rest.RestStatus;","+import org.elasticsearch.tasks.TaskId;","+import org.elasticsearch.test.ESIntegTestCase;","+import org.elasticsearch.test.SecurityIntegTestCase;","+import org.elasticsearch.test.SecuritySettingsSource;","+import org.elasticsearch.test.SecuritySettingsSourceField;","+import org.elasticsearch.transport.RemoteClusterAware;","+import org.elasticsearch.transport.TransportService;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.core.security.authc.Authentication;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.core.security.authc.AuthenticationField;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.core.security.authc.AuthenticationResult;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.core.security.authc.CrossClusterAccessSubjectInfo;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.core.security.authz.RoleDescriptor;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.core.security.authz.RoleDescriptorsIntersection;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.core.security.user.User;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.action.AbstractExternalDataSourceIT;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.action.EsqlCapabilities;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.action.EsqlQueryAction;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.action.EsqlQueryRequest;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.action.EsqlQueryResponse;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.core.expression.Attribute;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.core.expression.FieldAttribute;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.core.tree.Source;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.core.type.DataType;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.core.type.EsField;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.datasource.csv.CsvDataSourcePlugin;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.datasource.http.HttpDataSourcePlugin;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.datasources.ExternalSourceSettings;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.datasources.Federation;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.datasources.FileSplit;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.datasources.dataset.PutDatasetAction;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.datasources.datasource.PutDataSourceAction;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.datasources.datasource.TestEncryptionServicePlugin;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.datasources.spi.ExternalSplit;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.datasources.spi.FileList;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.datasources.spi.SimpleSourceMetadata;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.datasources.spi.StoragePath;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.plan.logical.ExternalRelation;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.plan.physical.ExchangeSinkExec;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.plan.physical.ExternalSourceExec;","+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.plan.physical.FragmentExec;","+import org.junit.Before;","+","+import java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets;","+import java.nio.file.Files;","+import java.nio.file.Path;","+import java.util.ArrayList;","+import java.util.Collection;","+import java.util.HashMap;","+import java.util.List;","+import java.util.Map;","+","+import static org.elasticsearch.test.hamcrest.ElasticsearchAssertions.assertAcked;","+import static org.elasticsearch.xpack.core.security.authc.support.UsernamePasswordToken.basicAuthHeaderValue;","+import static org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.EsqlTestUtils.TEST_CFG;","+import static org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.EsqlTestUtils.getValuesList;","+import static org.hamcrest.Matchers.contains;","+import static org.hamcrest.Matchers.containsString;","+import static org.hamcrest.Matchers.equalTo;","+import static org.hamcrest.Matchers.hasSize;","+import static org.hamcrest.Matchers.instanceOf;","+import static org.hamcrest.Matchers.is;","+","+/**","+ * A {@link DataNodeRequest} is authorized by the security filter on the {@code indices()} its sender chose, which says","+ * nothing about the dataset the {@link ExternalSourceExec} inside its plan names. The data node therefore decides for","+ * itself, from the plan, whether the request's credential may read that dataset, before it plans or rebinds anything","+ * ({@code DataNodeComputeHandler.messageReceived}). These tests send crafted requests straight to the data node action","+ * under users whose only difference is which dataset their role grants {@code read} on, and assert that the dataset","+ * is read when and only when the grant covers it, in both request shapes a coordinator sends (external splits, and","+ * shards with a plan that also reads a dataset).","+ */","+@ESIntegTestCase.ClusterScope(scope = ESIntegTestCase.Scope.SUITE, numDataNodes = 1, numClientNodes = 0)","+public class DataNodeRequestDatasetAuthorizationIT extends SecurityIntegTestCase {","+","+    private static final TimeValue TIMEOUT = TimeValue.timeValueSeconds(30);","+    private static final SecureString PASSWORD = new SecureString(SecuritySettingsSourceField.TEST_PASSWORD.toCharArray());","+","+    /** {@code read} on {@link #DATASET_A} and on {@link #INDEX}; nothing on {@link #DATASET_B}. */","+    private static final String READER = \"ds_reader\";","+    /** {@code read} on {@code pattern_*}, which covers {@link #DATASET_PATTERN} only by wildcard. */","+    private static final String PATTERN_READER = \"ds_pattern_reader\";","+    /** {@code read} on {@link #DATASET_A} under a DLS query. */","+    private static final String DLS_READER = \"ds_dls_reader\";","+    /** {@code read} on {@link #OTHER_INDEX} only: a credential allowed to send the compute action, with no dataset. */","+    private static final String INDEX_ONLY_READER = \"ds_index_only_reader\";","+","+    private static final String DATA_SOURCE = \"authz_ds\";","+    private static final String DATASET_A = \"authz_a\";","+    private static final String DATASET_B = \"authz_b\";","+    private static final String DATASET_PATTERN = \"pattern_authz\";","+    private static final String INDEX = \"authz_idx\";","+    private static final String OTHER_INDEX = \"authz_other_idx\";","+","+    private static Path fileA;","+    private static Path fileB;","+    private static Path filePattern;","+","+    @Override","+    protected String configUsers() {","+        StringBuilder users = new StringBuilder(super.configUsers());","+        for (String user : List.of(READER, PATTERN_READER, DLS_READER, INDEX_ONLY_READER)) {","+            users.append(user).append(':').append(SecuritySettingsSource.TEST_PASSWORD_HASHED).append('\\n');","+        }","+        return users.toString();","+    }","+","+    @Override","+    protected String configUsersRoles() {","+        StringBuilder usersRoles = new StringBuilder(super.configUsersRoles());","+        for (String user : List.of(READER, PATTERN_READER, DLS_READER, INDEX_ONLY_READER)) {","+            usersRoles.append(user).append(':').append(user).append('\\n');","+        }","+        return usersRoles.toString();","+    }","+","+    @Override","+    protected String configRoles() {","+        return super.configRoles() + \"\\n\" + \"\"\"","+            ds_reader:","+              indices:","+                - names: [ 'authz_a', 'authz_idx' ]","+                  privileges: [ 'read' ]","+            ds_pattern_reader:","+              indices:","+                - names: [ 'pattern_*' ]","+                  privileges: [ 'read' ]","+            ds_dls_reader:","+              indices:","+                - names: [ 'authz_a' ]","+                  privileges: [ 'read' ]","+                  query: '{\"match_all\": {}}'","+            ds_index_only_reader:","+              indices:","+                - names: [ 'authz_other_idx' ]","+                  privileges: [ 'read' ]","+            \"\"\";","+    }","+","+    @Override","+    protected Collection<Class<? extends Plugin>> nodePlugins() {","+        List<Class<? extends Plugin>> plugins = new ArrayList<>(super.nodePlugins());","+        // The same wiring as AbstractExternalDataSourceIT, on top of the security plugins the base class installs.","+        plugins.add(TestEncryptionServicePlugin.class);","+        plugins.add(AbstractExternalDataSourceIT.EsqlEnterpriseWithDatasourceExtensions.class);","+        plugins.add(HttpDataSourcePlugin.class);","+        plugins.add(AbstractExternalDataSourceIT.TestDataSourcePlugin.class);","+        plugins.add(CsvDataSourcePlugin.class);","+        return plugins;","+    }","+","+    @Override","+    protected Settings nodeSettings(int nodeOrdinal, Settings otherSettings) {","+        return Settings.builder()","+            .put(super.nodeSettings(nodeOrdinal, otherSettings))","+            .put(EsqlPlugin.QUERY_ALLOW_PARTIAL_RESULTS.getKey(), false)","+            .put(Federation.FEDERATION_ENABLED.getKey(), true)","+            .putList(ExternalSourceSettings.LOCAL_ALLOWED_PATHS.getKey(), createTempDir().getParent().toString())","+            .build();","+    }","+","+    /**","+     * Three datasets over three one-column CSV files, registered once with the superuser-like test user; the index","+     * the mixed-shape requests and queries read is recreated per test, as the cluster wipe drops it.","+     */","+    @Before","+    public void setupFixtures() throws Exception {","+        assumeTrue(\"requires dataset-in-from-command capability\", EsqlCapabilities.Cap.DATASET_IN_FROM_COMMAND.isEnabled());","+        assumeTrue(\"requires local filesystem feature flag\", HttpDataSourcePlugin.ESQL_EXTERNAL_DATASOURCES_LOCAL_FEATURE_FLAG.isEnabled());","+        if (fileA == null) {","+            Path dir = createTempDir();","+            fileA = Files.writeString(dir.resolve(\"a.csv\"), \"a\\na1\\na2\\n\", StandardCharsets.UTF_8);","+            fileB = Files.writeString(dir.resolve(\"b.csv\"), \"a\\nb1\\n\", StandardCharsets.UTF_8);","+            filePattern = Files.writeString(dir.resolve(\"pattern.csv\"), \"a\\np1\\n\", StandardCharsets.UTF_8);","+        }","+        registerDataSource();","+        registerDataset(DATASET_A, fileA);","+        registerDataset(DATASET_B, fileB);","+        registerDataset(DATASET_PATTERN, filePattern);","+        for (String index : List.of(INDEX, OTHER_INDEX)) {","+            assertAcked(","+                client().admin()","+                    .indices()","+                    .prepareCreate(index)","+                    .setSettings(","+                        Settings.builder().put(IndexMetadata.SETTING_NUMBER_OF_SHARDS, 1).put(IndexMetadata.SETTING_NUMBER_OF_REPLICAS, 0)","+                    )","+                    .setMapping(\"a\", \"type=keyword\")","+            );","+        }","+        client().prepareIndex(INDEX).setId(\"1\").setSource(\"a\", \"idx1\").get();","+        client().admin().indices().prepareRefresh(INDEX).get();","+        ensureGreen(INDEX, OTHER_INDEX);","+    }","+","+    public void testExternalRequestNamingAnUnauthorizedDatasetIsRefused() throws Exception {","+        assertRefused(sendExternal(READER, exec(DATASET_B, fileB)), DATASET_B);","+    }","+","+    public void testExternalRequestNamingAnAuthorizedDatasetReadsItsRegisteredDefinition() throws Exception {","+        // The exec carries a hostile config and another path; what is read is the registered definition of DATASET_A.","+        assertThat(sendExternal(READER, exec(DATASET_A, fileA)).expectRows(), contains(\"a1\", \"a2\"));","+    }","+","+    public void testUnregisteredDatasetIsRefusedLikeAnUnauthorizedOne() throws Exception {","+        Path never = createTempDir().resolve(\"never.csv\");","+        Files.writeString(never, \"a\\nn1\\n\", StandardCharsets.UTF_8);","+        assertRefused(sendExternal(READER, exec(\"authz_never_registered\", never)), \"authz_never_registered\");","+    }","+","+    public void testCredentialWithReadOnAnIndexButNotTheDatasetIsRefused() throws Exception {","+        // Allowed to send the compute action (read on an index), so the security filter lets the request through.","+        assertRefused(sendExternal(INDEX_ONLY_READER, exec(DATASET_A, fileA)), DATASET_A);","+    }","+","+    public void testRolePatternCoveringTheDatasetNameAuthorizesIt() throws Exception {","+        assertThat(sendExternal(PATTERN_READER, exec(DATASET_PATTERN, filePattern)).expectRows(), contains(\"p1\"));","+        assertRefused(sendExternal(PATTERN_READER, exec(DATASET_A, fileA)), DATASET_A);","+    }","+","+    public void testDlsOnTheDatasetIsRefused() throws Exception {","+        assertRefused(sendExternal(DLS_READER, exec(DATASET_A, fileA)), DATASET_A);","+    }","+","+    public void testShardRequestCarryingAnExternalSourceIsAuthorizedByTheDataset() throws Exception {","+        // READER may read INDEX, so the shard request passes the security filter in both cases; only the dataset differs.","+        assertThat(sendShard(READER, exec(DATASET_A, fileA)).expectRows(), contains(\"a1\", \"a2\"));","+        assertRefused(sendShard(READER, exec(DATASET_B, fileB)), DATASET_B);","+    }","+","+    /**","+     * The shape the shard path receives from a coordinator for {@code FROM idx, dataset}: the dataset is still a","+     * logical {@link ExternalRelation} inside the fragment. The name is found there too, and the accepted request","+     * reads the registered definition: the relation carries no splits, so the node lists the registered resource.","+     */","+    public void testShardRequestCarryingAnExternalRelationIsAuthorizedByTheDataset() throws Exception {","+        assertRefused(sendShard(READER, fragment(DATASET_B)), DATASET_B);","+        assertThat(sendShard(READER, fragment(DATASET_A)).expectRows(), contains(\"a1\", \"a2\"));","+    }","+","+    public void testCrossClusterAccessAuthenticationIsRefused() throws Exception {","+        // A cross-cluster credential whose grants cover the dataset name by pattern would otherwise be authorized.","+        Outcome outcome = send(crossClusterAccessAuthentication(), externalRequest(exec(DATASET_A, fileA)));","+        ElasticsearchStatusException refusal = outcome.refusal();","+        assertThat(refusal.getMessage(), containsString(\"local to the cluster that registered them\"));","+    }","+","+    public void testMalformedDatasetNamesAreRefused() throws Exception {","+        for (String name : List.of(\"\", \"*\", \"-\" + DATASET_A, DATASET_A + \",*\", \"remote:\" + DATASET_A)) {","+            assertRefused(sendExternal(READER, exec(name, fileA)), name);","+        }","+    }","+","+    public void testQueryingTheDatasetThroughTheCoordinatorStillWorks() throws Exception {","+        // Regression check that the coordinator's gate and the receiver's agree: the coordinator is the single data","+        // node, so its own data node request also passes through the receiver gate on the way to the rows. The refusal","+        // for INDEX_ONLY_READER is the coordinator's (Unknown index); the receiver gate is proven by the crafted cases.","+        try (EsqlQueryResponse response = query(READER, \"FROM \" + DATASET_A + \" | SORT a\")) {","+            assertThat(getValuesList(response), equalTo(List.of(List.of(\"a1\"), List.of(\"a2\"))));","+        }","+        try (EsqlQueryResponse response = query(READER, \"FROM \" + INDEX + \", \" + DATASET_A + \" | STATS c = COUNT(*)\")) {","+            assertThat(((Number) getValuesList(response).get(0).get(0)).longValue(), equalTo(3L));","+        }","+        Exception e = expectThrows(Exception.class, () -> query(INDEX_ONLY_READER, \"FROM \" + DATASET_A).close());","+        assertThat(ExceptionsHelper.unwrapCause(e).getMessage(), containsString(\"Unknown index [\" + DATASET_A + \"]\"));","+    }","+","+    /** What a request answered with: the rows it delivered to the exchange, or the refusal it ended with. */","+    private record Outcome(List<String> rows, Exception failure) {","+        ElasticsearchStatusException refusal() {","+            assertNotNull(\"expected a refusal but got rows \" + rows, failure);","+            Throwable cause = ExceptionsHelper.unwrapCause(failure);","+            assertThat(cause, instanceOf(ElasticsearchStatusException.class));","+            ElasticsearchStatusException refusal = (ElasticsearchStatusException) cause;","+            assertThat(refusal.status(), is(RestStatus.BAD_REQUEST));","+            return refusal;","+        }","+","+        List<String> expectRows() {","+            if (failure != null) {","+                throw new AssertionError(\"expected rows but the request failed\", failure);","+            }","+            return rows;","+        }","+    }","+","+    private static void assertRefused(Outcome outcome, String dataset) {","+        assertThat(outcome.refusal().getMessage(), containsString(\"external dataset [\" + dataset + \"] is not registered on this node\"));","+    }","+","+    private Outcome sendExternal(String user, ExternalSourceExec exec) {","+        return send(user, externalRequest(exec));","+    }","+","+    private Outcome sendShard(String user, ExternalSourceExec exec) {","+        return send(user, shardRequest(new ExchangeSinkExec(Source.EMPTY, exec.output(), false, exec)));","+    }","+","+    private Outcome sendShard(String user, FragmentExec fragment) {","+        return send(user, shardRequest(new ExchangeSinkExec(Source.EMPTY, fragment.output(), false, fragment)));","+    }","+","+    /**","+     * A transport request between nodes carries the authentication the coordinator established, not the credentials;","+     * the security sender interceptor insists on one being in the context. Each test user is a file-realm user whose","+     * single role has the user's name, so the authentication written here is what a coordinator would have forwarded.","+     */","+    private Outcome send(String user, DataNodeRequest request) {","+        Authentication authentication = Authentication.newRealmAuthentication(","+            new User(user, user),","+            new Authentication.RealmRef(\"file\", \"file\", \"coordinator\")","+        );","+        return send(authentication, request);","+    }","+","+    private Outcome send(Authentication authentication, DataNodeRequest request) {","+        return send(threadContext -> authentication.writeToContext(threadContext), request);","+    }","+","+    /**","+     * Sends {@code request} to the data node's own action, as a coordinator would, with the credential {@code credential}","+     * puts in the thread context, and drains the exchange the request writes to.","+     */","+    private Outcome send(CheckedConsumer<ThreadContext> credential, DataNodeRequest request) {","+        TransportService transportService = internalCluster().getDataNodeInstances(TransportService.class).iterator().next();","+        ExchangeService exchange = internalCluster().getInstance(ExchangeService.class, transportService.getLocalNode().getName());","+        ThreadContext threadContext = transportService.getThreadPool().getThreadContext();","+        String sessionId = request.sessionId();","+        // The coordinator opens the sink before it sends the request; without one the handler answers with an empty result.","+        ExchangeSinkHandler sink = exchange.createSinkHandler(sessionId, randomIntBetween(1, 4));","+        try {","+            request.setParentTask(new TaskId(transportService.getLocalNode().getId(), randomNonNegativeLong()));","+            PlainActionFuture<DataNodeComputeResponse> future = new PlainActionFuture<>();","+            try (ThreadContext.StoredContext ignored = threadContext.stashContext()) {","+                credential.accept(threadContext);","+                transportService.sendRequest(","+                    transportService.getLocalNode(),","+                    ComputeService.DATA_ACTION_NAME,","+                    request,","+                    new ActionListenerResponseHandler<>(","+                        future,","+                        in -> new DataNodeComputeResponse(in, threadContext),","+                        EsExecutors.DIRECT_EXECUTOR_SERVICE","+                    )","+                );","+            } catch (Exception e) {","+                return new Outcome(List.of(), e);","+            }","+            List<String> rows = new ArrayList<>();","+            Exception drainFailure = null;","+            try {","+                drain(sink, rows);","+            } catch (Exception e) {","+                // A refused request fails its sink; the failure the request answers with is the one that matters.","+                drainFailure = e;","+            }","+            try {","+                DataNodeComputeResponse response = future.actionGet(TIMEOUT);","+                assertThat(\"no shard-level failure expected\", response.shardLevelFailures().values(), hasSize(0));","+                if (drainFailure != null) {","+                    throw new AssertionError(\"the request succeeded but its pages could not be fetched\", drainFailure);","+                }","+                return new Outcome(rows, null);","+            } catch (Exception e) {","+                return new Outcome(rows, e);","+            }","+        } finally {","+            // A refused request has already failed and removed its sink; one that never reached the handler has not.","+            exchange.finishSinkHandler(sessionId, sink.isFinished() ? null : new IllegalStateException(\"test finished\"));","+        }","+    }","+","+    /** What one fetch from the sink delivered; the page is taken inside the fetch callback, before the sink releases the response. */","+    private record Fetched(@Nullable Page page, boolean finished) {}"],"additions":405,"deletions":0,"truncated":false}],"additions":541,"deletions":0,"truncated":true,"file_count":4},"error":null,"fetched_at":"2026-10-21T13:28:42.037604+00:00"}